            <ArticleTitle>Microwave-promoted facile access to 4-aminoquinoline-phthalimides: Synthesis and anti-plasmodial evaluation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>150-156</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0223-5234(17)30936-4</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ejmech.2017.11.033</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Microwave promoted high yielding synthesis of 4-aminoquinoline-phthalimides was developed with an aim to evaluate their anti-plasmodial potential. The scaffolds with longer spacer length (n = 6, 8) between two pharmacophores and a halogen substituent on the phthalimide ring displayed good antiplasmodial activity. Compound 5w, with an optimum combination of hexyl chain as spacer along with a tetra-bromophthalimide ring proved to be most potent and non-cytotoxic among the series exhibiting an IC50 value of 0.10 μM.</AbstractText>
